<Base title="About Us">
	<h1 class="sd-text-headline">About the Department</h1>
	<p>
		The Department of Second Drafts was founded by writers, for writers. We manage a workstation for storytellers: novelists, essayists,
		screenwriters, Substackers, researchers, poets, cartoonists, copywriters. Long-form, short-form, formless, forms that don't exist yet.
	</p>
	<p>
		Writing is deeply personal, and everyone does it differently. Some writers need to keep detailed research notes,
		build an outline with pointers to those notes, cite their sources, transcribe their interviews. Some need their
		complex plot to be checked for gaps before a reader finds them. Some need to build a whole world, to create people
		and places and rules that hold together. Some just need dark mode. Our goal is to
		create tools you can pick up one at a time and use however you like.
	</p>
	<p>
		Why second drafts? Most writing exists to be shared, and getting a piece ready for an audience can be daunting and
		difficult. In some ways, this is where the real work of writing begins.
	</p>
	<p>We're here to help with that.</p>
</Base>

